{"path":"experimental/fs/recursive_directory_iterator/increment","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator::operator++, increment","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::experimental::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator::</span>operator++, increment","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/experimental/fs/recursive_directory_iterator/increment","section":"experimental","kind":"page","summary":"Advances the iterator to the next entry.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">recursive_directory_iterator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> operator<span class=\"sy2\">++</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-fs_ts\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">recursive_directory_iterator<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> increment<span class=\"br0\">(</span> error_code<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> ec <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-fs-ts t-mark-ts\">(filesystem TS)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Advances the iterator to the next entry.\n</p><p>If there are no more entries left in the currently iterated directory, the iteration is resumed over the parent directory. The process is repeated if the parent directory has no sibling entries that can to be iterated on. If the parent of the directory hierarchy that has been recursively iterated on is reached (there are no candidate entries at <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">depth<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> is set to an end iterator.\n</p><p>Otherwise, if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> refers to a directory, it is iterated into if the following conditions are met:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/experimental/fs/recursive_directory_iterator/disable_recursion_pending\">disable_recursion_pending()</a></span> has not been called before this increment, i.e. <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">recursion_pending<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>.\n</li><li> The directory is not a symlink or following symlinks is enabled, i.e. \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy3\">!</span>is_symlink<span class=\"br0\">(</span>this<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>symlink_status<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">||</span></span><br><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"br0\">(</span>options<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> directory_options<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">follow_directory_symlink</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</dd></dl>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> ec\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> error code to store the error status to\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Exceptions\">Exceptions</h3>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">1)</span> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">filesystem_error</span></code> if an error occurs. The error code is set to an appropriate error code for the error that caused the failure.</div>\n<div class=\"t-li1\"><span class=\"t-li\">2)</span> <div class=\"t-noexcept-inline\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/noexcept_spec\"><code>noexcept</code></a> specification:&nbsp;&nbsp;<div class=\"t-noexcept-box\"><span class=\"t-cc\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span></span></span></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;</div></div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Exceptions","id":"Exceptions"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"experimental","title":"Experimental C++ Features"},{"path":"experimental/fs","title":"Filesystem library"},{"path":"experimental/fs/recursive_directory_iterator","title":"std::experimental::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::experimental::filesystem::recursive_directory_iterator::operator++, increment","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations. Advances the iterator to the next entry."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"ec"},{"label":"Return value","note":"*this"},{"label":"Exceptions","note":"filesystem_error if an error occurs. The error code is set to an appropriate error code for the error that caused the failure."}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":177,"codeBlockCount":0}
